What this fork replaced
- Visual identity: the name, the Kip mark (src/shared/logo.ts) and the KIP DECK wordmark, the color and type tokens
  (src/client/styles/tokens.css), the icon set (src/client/ui/icons.ts), the fonts' selection
  (Archivo and JetBrains Mono, OFL, with their licenses in src/client/styles/fonts/).
- The 3D scene: the deck's plan (src/shared/layout.ts), its materials and light, the units and
  operators, the boards' look, the Proof corner and the merge beat.
- The interface: the top bar and its counters, the Units rail, the mission strip, Mission control,
  the menu's grouping, the toasts, the 2D view's Plot, the sign-in pages, the loading card and the
  /pom/ Proof ledger with its share card.
- The copy: product wording, the deck's verbs (deploy, stand down) and server messages.
- New features: the inbox at / (it replaced the 2D view), mission control (attention ranking, goals and milestones, review inbox, timeline,
  reminders) and Proof of Merge on testnets (Solana devnet bounty escrow, Base Sepolia EAS
  attestations, ERC-8004 reputation, x402 paid tasks, the public showcase).

What remains from upstream
- The server's architecture: floors (decks), workers and their terminals, git worktrees, the
  provider adapters, the task queue, meetings (the Review bay), voice and screen sharing, the
  whiteboard, accounts and sign-ins, the tunnel and the installers.
- The client's architecture: the registries, the state store and its slices, the player and its
  camera, the navigation grid and the modal frame.
- The agent-office command, kept as an alias of kipdeck so upstream's scripts keep working.
